language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Dudeney number: a perfect cube, larger than 1, with at most n digits, whose digit sum equals its cube root.
given n : int(1..)
find number : int(2..10**n-1)
$ the decimal digits of the number, the first digit is the units digit
find digits : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..9)
$ the cube root of the number
find root : int(2..1000)
branching on [root, digits]
such that
$ the number is the cube of its root
number = root * root * root,
$ the digits, weighted by their place value, make up the number
number = (sum k : int(1..n) . digits[k] * 10**(k-1)),
$ the sum of the digits equals the cube root
root = (sum k : int(1..n) . digits[k])
